## A diverging binned gradient

```r
# Get a divergent binned scale with the *2 variant
ggplot(df, aes(x, y)) +
  geom_point(aes(colour = z1)) +
  scale_colour_steps2()
```

```elixir
df
|> Plot.new(%{x: :x, y: :y})
|> Plot.geom_point(%{colour: :z1})
|> Plot.scale_color_steps2()
|> render.()
```

## Colours of your own

```r
# Define your own colour ramp to extract binned colours from
ggplot(df, aes(x, y)) +
  geom_point(aes(colour = z1)) +
  scale_colour_stepsn(colours = terrain.colors(10))
```

R's `terrain.colors(10)` is written out as the ten colours it returns.

```elixir
terrain =
  ~w(#00A600 #2DB600 #63C600 #A0D600 #E6E600 #E8C32E #EBB25E #EDB48E #F0C9C0 #F2F2F2)

df
|> Plot.new(%{x: :x, y: :y})
|> Plot.geom_point(%{colour: :z1})
|> Plot.scale_color_stepsn(colors: terrain)
|> render.()
```